+# The Daily Grind
+
+The static page loads the autonomous `<coffee-card>` custom element from
+`components/coffee-card.js`. Each card owns its shadow DOM and styles, inherits the
+page's font and theme variables, and updates in place when attributes change.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card name="Maple Oat Latte" description="Oat milk and maple syrup."
+  href="/menu/seasonal" price="4.50" featured></coffee-card>
+```
+
+All supported attributes have matching JavaScript properties:
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name`, `description`, `href` | String | `''` |
+| `price` | Non-negative finite number (USD) | `null` (hidden) |
+| `featured`, `disabled` | Boolean | `false` |
+
+Setting properties reflects back to attributes; changing or removing attributes
+updates properties and rendering. Set strings or price to `null`/`undefined` to
+remove them. Invalid price attributes hide the price; invalid price property
+assignments throw `RangeError`. Zero is a valid price.
+
+Boolean attributes follow HTML presence semantics: `disabled="false"` still
+disables the card. Use `card.disabled = false` or remove the attribute to enable
+it. Disabled cards (or cards without a destination) expose a disabled link and
+prevent navigation. `featured` adds an accent outline.
+
+Connection upgrades properties assigned before registration and attaches the
+click listener. Disconnection removes it; reconnection restores it. Attribute
+updates preserve the internal nodes and keyboard focus.
+
+Run the automated DOM tests with `pnpm test`. No server is required.
